{"step_index":49,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T04:58:43Z","input_tokens":1110,"cache_read_tokens":134363,"output_tokens":897,"thinking":"I'm checking how the merged quads' normals get oriented: flipping everything when the summed z is negative handles the single-quad case, but bmesh's recalc on disconnected islands might leave them mixed. Per-object recalc followed by a flip only when nz is negative would avoid that, so I'm weighing whether it guarantees every piece ends up facing up.\n\nI'm weighing whether mixed normals across the disconnected quads could show up in shading, since the sum-based flip might leave some faces pointing down. Rather than rely on recalc, I'm planning a post-fix in Parts.build that flips only the individual faces whose normal z is negative.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"d:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\v5_env.py\"","Replacement":"\"    def build(self, up=False):\\n        if not self.f:\\n            return None\\n        ob = mesh_from(self.name, self.v, self.f, self.mats, face_mat=self.fm, up=up)\\n        if up:      # 多个互不相连的平面片：逐面保证朝上（recalc 只能保证每个岛内一致）\\n            me = ob.data\\n            bm = bmesh.new()\\n            bm.from_mesh(me)\\n            down = [f for f in bm.faces if f.normal.z < 0]\\n            if down:\\n                bmesh.ops.reverse_faces(bm, faces=down)\\n                bm.to_mesh(me)\\n                me.update()\\n            bm.free()\\n        return ob\"","Target":"\"    def build(self, up=False):\\n        if not self.f:\\n            return None\\n        return mesh_from(self.name, self.v, self.f, self.mats, face_mat=self.fm, up=up)\""}}]}
