ild halved them: int(L/14), int(L/40)). Every origin sits at its bbox center.\\n2. FencePosts: ±0.07 m along the tangent, 486 real quads. 3. FieldMasts: faces use base+i. 4. Brake poles: ±0.32 m along the tangent, merged per group into V5_Brake_{i}_Poles.\\n5. Per stand: _Trusses (86 beams total, front→back roof edge, 0.16 m), _Columns, _FrontPosts, _Flagpoles and _Flags (multi-material: V5_Flag_0..4) are each ONE mesh. V5_PitBoxLine_* → V5_PitBoxLines (60 quads, all faces up). 0 loose verts, 0 duplicate faces, 0 zero-area faces in V5_ meshes.\\n6. 21 Empties (ARROWS, Z-rotation = track heading, at ground center): V5_Stand_{Main,T1,Mid,Complex,South,Club}, V5_Bridge_A/B, V5_Screen_A/B, V5_Brake_0..2, V5_Marshal_0..6, V5_Gantry (posts, beam, banner, 5 start lights). Children use parent_inverse = I and matrix_basis = parent⁻¹·world, so their location reads relative to the Empty. My move test: all children follow exactly. Removed empty collections 09_Studio_Stage_Rig and WheelSpokes_FL/FR/RL/RR. Renamed objects to avoid clashing with the Empty names: Stand_X_{i}→Stand_X_Tier{i}, Screen_A→Screen_A_Panel (+_Legs), Bridge_A→Bridge_A_Deck (+_Pier\n<truncated 877 bytes>"}},{"name":"swarm_wait","args":{"since":"6"}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
